-- title:
--   Regular differentials inject into weight-2 cusp forms for Γ(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$, and let $K$ be a field that is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an algebra over [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) — the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by `jAnalytic` together with all the functions `fricke N v` for $v : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ with $v \neq 0$ — such that the two algebra structures are compatible (the scalar tower $\mathbb{C} \to$ `ring N` $\to K$) and $K$ is a fraction field of `ring N`. The assertion is that there exists an injective $\mathbb{C}$-linear map from [`AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials.html#L26) to `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma N) 2`. Here `regularDifferentials ℂ K` is the $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of the Kähler differentials $\Omega_{K/\mathbb{C}}$ consisting of those $\omega$ such that for every place $v$ of $K$ over $\mathbb{C}$ — that is, every valuation subring of $K$ which contains the image of $\mathbb{C}$, is not all of $K$, and is a principal ideal ring — one has $\omega = f \cdot \mathrm{d}t_v$ for some $f$ in that valuation subring, where $t_v$ is the chosen uniformiser of $v$; and `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma N) 2` is the space of holomorphic weight-$2$ cusp forms for the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(N)$.
--
--   This is the injection of the differentials of the first kind on the modular curve of level $N$, presented as the function field $K$ of the algebra generated by $j$ and the Fricke functions, into the weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma(N)$; classically the map is $\omega = h\,\mathrm{d}j \mapsto h \cdot j'/(2\pi i)$. It is used in the bound relating $12g - 12$ plus a cusp contribution to the dimension of $S_2(\Gamma(N))$, via [`ModularCurve.twelve_mul_add_mul_index_le_finrank_cuspForm_Gamma`](thm.html#ModularCurve.twelve_mul_add_mul_index_le_finrank_cuspForm_Gamma).
